[{:adr/authoritative_for ["cloud-itonami-isic-5820 vs Salesforce coverage assessment" "crm.llm-realmodel/real-advisor live-model verification"], :adr/topic "cloud-itonami-isic-5820-salesforce-coverage-real-advisor-verify", :adr/related ["adr-2607172600" "adr-2607172500" "adr-2607173100"], :adr/status "accepted", :adr/id "adr-2607173300-isic-5820-salesforce-coverage-real-advisor-verify", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/last_verified "2026-07-17", :adr/body "# ADR-2607173300: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 (Salesforce-replace CRM) -- coverage/maturity assessment + real-advisor live wiring\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-17\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (owner directive: \\\"haisen \u3082\u9032\u3081\u3066, \u4eca\u306e salesforce \u306b\u5bfe\u3059\u308b\u5b9f\u88c5 coverage, \u6210\u719f\u5ea6\u306f?\\\")\n**Scope**: assessment only (read `orgs/kotoba-lang/crm` + `orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5820`), plus one code change (`dev/real_advisor_check.clj` + docstring, child repo `f479d732e731`) + west pin advance (`c75aa82922d2`).\n\n## Coverage assessment vs Salesforce (factual, not scored)\n\n**What's real and working** (`kotoba-lang/crm`: 4 files/465 lines/25 tests; `isic-5820`: 11 files/1985 lines/76 tests):\n- 5-stage linear pipeline stage-transition validator (forward-only, no-skip) -- real, tested.\n- ASC 606/IFRS 15 revenue recognition -- **straight-line, single-obligation only**. No usage billing, contract mods, multi-element allocation.\n- 6 governor gates (RBAC, discount-authority, entitlement-scope, double-close, stage-sequence, source-provenance) + 2 soft gates -- all real, individually unit-tested.\n- Funnel/conversion analytics -- **point-in-time snapshot only**, no stage-history log, no cohort/time dimension.\n- Data model: **4 entity types** (rep, account, opportunity, subscription) + append-only ledger. **No Contact, no Lead, no Task/Activity, no custom-field mechanism** -- store's own docstring: \\\"NO field anywhere in this schema for marketing-campaign attribution or support-ticket SLA.\\\"\n- HTTP service: real http-kit server, constant-time bearer auth, 4 endpoints, fail-closed. Self-declared: single-process, single-tenant, no TLS termination, no rate limiting.\n- Durable storage: only `file_store.clj` (flat-file EDN, not multi-writer-safe). `DatomicStore` is a non-durable in-process atom by its own admission.\n\n**What's explicitly out of scope** (`docs/business-model.md` \\\"Honest scope (R0)\\\" + \\\"Sibling-actor roadmap\\\", confirmed by code-wide grep = zero hits): marketing automation (campaigns/email sequences/lead scoring -- a `leadscore.cljc` exists in the shared `kotoba-lang/crm` lib but is wired to ZERO consumers, built for a not-yet-built sibling actor), customer-service/ticketing (cases/SLA/KB), multi-currency (amounts hardcoded `-usd`), territory management, workflow-approval chains beyond the single pipeline, BI/custom-report builder (only a funnel rollup + single-record disclosure exist), integration/API marketplace.\n\n**Production readiness**: no CI (`.github/workflows`) in either repo. No live deployed CRM product instance -- the \\\"live now\\\" claim in business-model.md is a Stripe *billing* checkout link (managed-hosting sale), not a running product URL. No test in either repo previously exercised a real external model call (fixed by this ADR, see below).\n\n**Reading**: 5820 covers the governed sales-pipeline + entitlement-enforcement CORE of Salesforce (the part this fleet's actor pattern is designed to seal), and explicitly, deliberately does NOT cover the surrounding suite (marketing, service, reporting depth, multi-tenant/multi-currency ops) -- by design, not by gap-that-should-be-closed today (sibling actors are the documented path for those). Within its declared scope, the implementation is real (not stubbed) and reasonably tested (101 combined `deftest` across both repos), but has never run against production traffic or a real model until this ADR.\n\n## Wiring change: real-advisor live verification (closes a real gap)\n\n`crm.llm-realmodel/real-advisor`'s own docstring admitted: \\\"a real end-to-end call... has NEVER been exercised\\\" (no API credentials existed in any sandbox this file was built in). This ADR closes that gap using the repo-wide `murakumo-main` SSoT alias (ADR-2607173100):\n\n- Added `dev/real_advisor_check.clj` (mirrors `cloud-itonami-isic-6399/dev/real_advisor_check.clj`'s established pattern; not part of CI, needs a live token) to isic-5820.\n- Ran it live: `provider :anthropic`, `url https://api.murakumo.cloud/v1/messages`, `model murakumo-main` (currently resolves to qwen3.6-35b-a3b).\n- **Scenario A** (nonexistent opportunity `opp-1`): model correctly reasons the opportunity is nil, returns a well-formed EDN proposal, actor graph routes it, governor HOLDs (correct -- no real transition possible).\n- **Scenario B** (real seeded `opp-100`, `:prospecting` stage): model returns a well-formed `:stage-transition-upsert` proposal with sensible summary/rationale, confidence 0.9, correctly parsed as EDN, routed through the exact same actor graph the mock advisor uses.\n- Updated `llm_realmodel.clj`'s docstring to record verified status (child commit `f479d732e731`, west pin advanced `f2ba51d21d74`\u2192`f479d732e731`, `c75aa82922d2`).\n\n## Consequences\n\n- 5820's RevOps-LLM advisor seam is now proven end-to-end against a real model, not just a local stub -- an operator supplying `ISIC5820_MODEL_API_KEY` (or wiring `murakumo-main`) gets genuinely verified behavior, not merely \\\"genuinely wired but unverified\\\" as before.\n- Coverage gaps (marketing automation, ticketing, multi-currency, deeper reporting) remain intentionally unbuilt per the sibling-actor roadmap -- not addressed by this ADR, flagged here for the owner's prioritization.\n", :adr/deciders ["Jun Kawasaki"], :adr/date "2026-07-17", :db/id -1, :adr/authoritative true, :adr/title "ADR-2607173300: cloud-itonami-isic-5820 Salesforce-parity coverage assessment + real-advisor live wiring", :adr/source-format "edn"}]